# No deferrals without the operator's explicit word

**Default: finish it.** When the operator asks for a complete outcome ("port the whole page", "do
the whole plan"), **ship the whole outcome**. Do not invent deferrals. This is `CLAUDE.md` law 1.

## The only legal deferral

The operator **explicitly** says, in this conversation (or in a quoted earlier message they
reaffirm), words like:

- "defer X"
- "skip X"
- "not this pass — X later"
- "MVP only — leave Y"

**Quote that authorization** in the verify log or the commit body. No quote → **not deferred**.
Work the operator deferred is recorded as a ticket with status `deferred`
(`cargo xtask ticket set-status <id> deferred`), never as `shipped`.

Soft plan prose ("if feasible", "optional", "P1 later", "fold forward", "record as follow-up") is
**not** authorization — including when **you** wrote that prose into the plan.

## Forbidden (these are failures, not process)

```text
❌ "Folded forward" / "deferred to <another ticket>" / "follow-on" for in-scope work
❌ Shipping an MVP and calling the program or slice "complete" while listed scope remains
❌ Writing your own "Out of scope" / "Deferred" section to shrink an operator "do everything" ask
❌ "Document as deferred" in a verify log instead of implementing
❌ A partial ship plus "the operator can do the rest later" without explicit defer approval
❌ Treating audit P0/P1 labels as permission to skip P1 when the ask was a complete cutover
```

```text
✅ Implement every item the operator's ask, the approved plan's scope and the acceptance matrix require
✅ If truly blocked (secrets, Workbench down, missing GPU): STOP and ASK — do not invent a deferral ticket and mark the work done
✅ Defer only after the operator says "defer X" / "skip X this pass"
```

## Plans and audits

When drafting a finish plan: **do not pre-load deferrals**. List the remaining work as
**must-do**. If something might need the operator's judgment, **ask before** writing "fold
forward" into the plan. A plan that ships with a Deferred appendix the operator never approved is
non-compliant.

## Specs, plans, handoffs and prompts

- Do **not** put "fold forward X" or "out of scope: do Y later" in a spec, plan, handoff or prompt
  unless the operator already authorized that deferral.
- A prompt's `═══ DO NOT ═══` section may ban unrelated lanes; it must **not** silently drop the
  operator's complete-outcome ask.

## Who it binds

Every agent, whatever product runs it, and every person: planners, coding agents, slice agents,
orchestrators and auditors. It grants no permission to write code — the modes in
[`cursor-agent-workflow.mdc`](/.cursor/rules/cursor-agent-workflow.mdc) decide that.
